# .host-software — the Where room recipe (STRUCTURE.md). One stanza per
# component: source URL, the pinned canonical SHA, the canonical branch, any
# parallel-line worktrees, and the reproducibility record.
#
# The crate migrated 2026-09-13 (component cb7bfb4) from the former
# rope-agentic monorepo (tools/ds-lite-punch/), unmodified; the musl
# release build reproduces the deployed artifact byte-identically, so the
# waiver (call/0012) is retired by call/0016.
[software "ds-lite-punch"]
	url   = https://github.com/slartibardfast/ds-lite-punch.git
	pin   = 3ae0abf91aab765aa6b589f818c6fe265d063e77
	branch = main
	toolchain = ghcr.io/rust-cross/rust-musl-cross@sha256:ce75e9174325d4fbb3de85c309e2d7ca29f7500169bc4b5d2c611ff7e86d549a
	build = cargo build --release --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl
	artifact = target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/ds-lite-punch 0a9ae280c8dc1d8fc01b6d1248b4401a40d2ae9853233e067ed2c9f7d5a53f23
# The toolchain is a digest-pinned container rather than a target triple:
# `--verify-build` runs the recorded `build` inside it, so the image is what
# reproduces the artifact and a movable tag would invalidate every hash
# recorded under it. The hash above was produced inside that image for the
# tagged commit, by the component's own lane and again by the Release lane, with
# the runs agreeing byte for byte; an anonymous fetch of the release asset
# hashes to the same value, and the release publishes that binary, so a
# deployment takes those bytes rather than a local build's (call/0032). A
# version bump moves those bytes from 0.2.0 on: `--version` prints the crate
# version, so the string is compiled into the binary, and the pin therefore
# names the commit that carries the bump, which is also the commit the tag
# points at (call/0036).
#
# This development host has no container runtime, so its own target/ builds
# with the ambient compiler and hashes differently. That is a property of the
# host, not a defect in the record: a local build is for iteration, and the
# binary on the test router was installed from the lane's artifact and checked
# against the hash above before it was started.
